theorem.content:
\label{th:cfs}
For a fixed value of $x$, we consider the function which maps the tree to the set of values given by evaluating every vertex at this value of $x$.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Setting a value $x>0$ injectively maps the tree to a dense subset of $(0,1)$.
        \item Setting a value $x>0$ bijectively maps the tree to $\mathbb{Q} \cap (0,1)$ if and only if $x \in \mathbb{Z}^+$.
    \end{enumerate}

