[{\cite[Theorem~0.1]{AFKKZ13}}] \label{FIT.th}
Let \( X \) be an affine variety. Then the following are equivalent:  
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \( X \) is flexible;  
  \item \( \SAut(X) \) acts transitively on the smooth locus \( X^\mathrm{reg} \);  
  \item if \( \dim X \ge 2 \), \( \SAut(X) \) acts infinitely transitively on \( X^\mathrm{reg} \).
\end{enumerate}

